    p6,p7=man['maps']['floor6'],man['maps']['floor7'];mix=man['mixvpr'];sp=man['superpoint']
    lines=['# P0 — Static resource / compatibility audit: all-online K210 localization','', '**Scope:** read-only resource-first audit. Every number has a label: `MEASURED`, `COMPILER_REPORTED`, `DERIVED_EXACT`, `ESTIMATED`, or `UNKNOWN`. File sizes and array shapes were measured from existing artifacts; no board RAM value is claimed. **Within tables, every numeric cell inherits the single label in its row unless the cell itself specifies a different label.**','', '## Executive decision','', '**FULL PIPELINE STATIC FEASIBILITY: RESOURCE RISK**','', 'The decisive existing evidence is frozen MixVPR M0.3: nncase import/PTQ/compile passed, but K210 gencode failed with `Allocator has ran out of memory`. This is a confirmed compiler resource risk, **not** a measured general-SRAM peak. SuperPoint compiles for both candidates, but cannot remove the MixVPR blocker.','', '## 1. Frozen target and compatibility','', '| Component | Current evidence | Status | First blocker |','|---|---|---|---|','| Camera | no board camera configuration inspected | UNKNOWN | sensor format/resolution/buffer placement unknown |','| MixVPR preprocessing | M0.1 real-image parity PASS | PASS | external preprocessing needs board implementation measurement |','| MixVPR backbone | standalone nncase import PASS | PASS (import only) | full core resource path still fails later |','| MixVPR aggregator | M0.3 import PASS after canonicalization | PASS (import only) | full gencode allocator OOM |','| MixVPR PTQ | M0.3 PASS | PASS | — |','| MixVPR gencode | M0.3 FAIL | RED | `Allocator has ran out of memory` |','| Global retrieval | current FP16 DB files measured | PLAUSIBLE storage/streaming model | K210 SD and numeric-kernel behavior unmeasured |','| SuperPoint V1-FR12 | 160/192 compiler gencode PASS | PASS (compiler) | board runtime/AI memory unknown |','| Point3D matching | current algorithm audited | PARTIAL | C/C++ streaming implementation/throughput unmeasured |','| PnP | pycolmap absolute-pose call identified | UNKNOWN | K210 solver/workspace not audited |','| UART | small payload only | PLAUSIBLE | board driver/protocol unknown |','', '## 2. Camera and preprocessing ledger','', '| Buffer | Shape / representation | Bytes | Label | Lifetime / reuse |','|---|---|---:|---|---|', '| Capture frame | camera DVP output | — | UNKNOWN | sensor mode/resolution not frozen; do not assume coexistence with derived buffers |','| RGB565 | camera-dependent | — | UNKNOWN | may be capture format; only reuse after conversion if driver permits |',f"| RGB888 resize staging | 320×320×3 | {320*320*3:,} | DERIVED_EXACT | can be released once FP32 MixVPR input is made; does not need coexist with SuperPoint input |",f"| MixVPR normalized input | 1×3×320×320 FP32 | {mix['input_fp32_bytes']['value']:,} | DERIVED_EXACT | live through MixVPR inference; sequential with SuperPoint |",f"| SuperPoint grayscale primary | 1×1×120×160 | {160*120:,} | DERIVED_EXACT | can be produced after MixVPR input/output phase and reused as a scratch buffer |",f"| SuperPoint grayscale fallback | 1×1×144×192 | {144*192:,} | DERIVED_EXACT | alternative only; not concurrent with 160×120 |",'', 'A camera capture buffer may overlap a conversion destination only if the driver proves it. That placement is **UNKNOWN**, therefore it is excluded from every numeric peak below rather than guessed.','', '## 3. MixVPR resource ledger','', f"- Parameters: {mix['parameters']['value']:,} (`DERIVED_EXACT`); FP32 weights {kb(mix['fp32_parameter_bytes']['value'])} (`DERIVED_EXACT`); theoretical INT8 {kb(mix['int8_parameter_bytes_theoretical']['value'])} (`DERIVED_EXACT`).",f"- Input {kb(mix['input_fp32_bytes']['value'])} (`DERIVED_EXACT`); descriptor FP32 {kb(mix['descriptor_fp32_bytes']['value'])}, INT8 comparison {kb(mix['descriptor_int8_comparison_bytes']['value'])} (`DERIVED_EXACT`).",f"- Largest logical activation: `{mix['largest_logical']['value']['name']}` {mix['largest_logical']['value']['shape']} = {kb(mix['largest_logical']['value']['fp32_bytes'])} FP32 / {kb(mix['largest_logical']['value']['projected_int8_bytes'])} projected INT8 (`DERIVED_EXACT`; not runtime peak).",f"- Backbone logical largest: `{mix['largest_backbone_logical']['value']['name']}` {kb(mix['largest_backbone_logical']['value']['fp32_bytes'])}; aggregator logical largest: `{mix['largest_aggregator_logical']['value']['name']}` {kb(mix['largest_aggregator_logical']['value']['fp32_bytes'])} (`DERIVED_EXACT`).",'- Model storage: no MixVPR kmodel exists. M0.3 gencode allocator OOM is `COMPILER_REPORTED`; workspace/AI SRAM amount is `UNKNOWN`.','', '## 4. Actual map, retrieval, covisibility, and Point3D index','', '| Existing package | Refs / global dtype | Global descriptors | H5 file | Indexed Point3D rows | Index file | COLMAP images / points / cameras |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
    for p in (p6,p7):
        g=p['global_db'];a={x['name']:x for x in p['point3d_index']['arrays']};c=p['colmap']['counts_from_binary_headers'];lines.append(f"| {p['package']} | {g['reference_count']:,} / FP16 4096-D | {kb(g['logical_descriptor_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(g['file_bytes'])} `MEASURED` | {a['descriptors']['shape'][0]:,} | {kb(p['point3d_index']['file_bytes'])} `MEASURED` | {c['images']:,} / {c['points3D']:,} / {c['cameras']:,} `MEASURED` |")
    lines += ['', 'Global DB FP32/FP16/INT8 logical storage (`DERIVED_EXACT`):', '', '| Package | FP32 | Current FP16 | INT8 comparison |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
    for p in (p6,p7):
        n=p['global_db']['reference_count'];lines.append(f"| {p['package']} | {kb(n*4096*4)} | {kb(n*4096*2)} | {kb(n*4096)} |")
    lines += ['', 'The current Python implementation loads DB arrays and builds covisibility from a `pycolmap.Reconstruction`. For K210 feasibility, SD/flash streaming is conceptually possible for reference descriptors and Point3D descriptor blocks, but an online compact covisibility/image→Point3D representation does not exist yet: its RAM and I/O are `UNKNOWN`. Current files remain offline storage; this audit does not redesign them.','', '### Retrieval streaming working set','', 'Assumes current FP16 reference records are staged blockwise; query FP32 + FP16 block + FP32 block scores + top-9 `(id,score)`. It excludes any conversion/kernel scratch, which is `UNKNOWN`.', '', '| Block refs | Bytes | Label |','|---:|---:|---|']
    for b,v in man['retrieval_streaming_work'].items():lines.append(f'| {b} | {kb(v)} | DERIVED_EXACT for listed buffers |')
    lines += ['', '### Point3D index content (current NPZ arrays)','', '| Package | descriptors | xyz | point IDs | extra metadata arrays |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for p in (p6,p7):
        a={x['name']:x for x in p['point3d_index']['arrays']};extra=sum(x['bytes'] for x in p['point3d_index']['arrays'] if x['name'] not in ('descriptors','xyz','point_ids'));lines.append(f"| {p['package']} | {a['descriptors']['shape']} {a['descriptors']['dtype']} {kb(a['descriptors']['bytes'])} | {a['xyz']['shape']} {a['xyz']['dtype']} {kb(a['xyz']['bytes'])} | {a['point_ids']['shape']} {a['point_ids']['dtype']} {kb(a['point_ids']['bytes'])} | {kb(extra)} |")
    lines += ['', 'Index storage comparison (`DERIVED_EXACT`, descriptors only):', '', '| Package | FP32 current logical | FP16 comparison | INT8 comparison |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
    for p in (p6,p7):
        a={x['name']:x for x in p['point3d_index']['arrays']};n=a['descriptors']['shape'][0];lines.append(f'| {p["package"]} | {kb(n*256*4)} | {kb(n*256*2)} | {kb(n*256)} |')
    lines += ['', 'Current host implementation warning: `Point3DDescriptorIndex.__init__()` uses `np.load()` then materializes the complete descriptors (FP32), xyz (FP32), xz copy (FP32) and point IDs (I64). It therefore is not a K210-RAM implementation. The C/C++ block-streaming rows below are an `ESTIMATED` feasibility model retaining the same matching semantics, not a claim that the current Python object fits.', '', '## 5. SuperPoint ledger','', '| Resolution | kmodel | compiler TOTAL | input | dense detector | dense descriptor map | largest logical FP32 / projected INT8 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|',f"| 160×120 primary | {kb(sp['160x120']['kmodel_bytes'])} `MEASURED` | {kb(859784)} `COMPILER_REPORTED` | {kb(sp['160x120']['detector_dense']['fp32_bytes']*0+160*120)} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(sp['160x120']['detector_dense']['fp32_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(sp['160x120']['descriptor_dense']['fp32_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(sp['160x120']['largest_logical_fp32_bytes'])} / {kb(sp['160x120']['largest_logical_int8_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` |",f"| 192×144 fallback | {kb(sp['192x144']['kmodel_bytes'])} `MEASURED` | {kb(1113880)} `COMPILER_REPORTED` | {kb(192*144)} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(sp['192x144']['detector_dense']['fp32_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(sp['192x144']['descriptor_dense']['fp32_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` | {kb(sp['192x144']['largest_logical_fp32_bytes'])} / {kb(sp['192x144']['largest_logical_int8_bytes'])} `DERIVED_EXACT` |",'', 'Dense detector/descriptor maps can be released after NMS, Top-K and descriptor sampling produces the selected feature set. They do not need to coexist with Point3D streaming matching; the selected coordinates/scores/descriptors remain.','', '| Selected K | FP32 coords+score+256-D desc | INT8 descriptor comparison | Label |','|---:|---:|---:|---|']
    for k,v in man['selected_feature_storage'].items():lines.append(f"| {k} | {kb(v['fp32_descriptor_bytes'])} | {kb(v['int8_comparison_bytes'])} | DERIVED_EXACT |")
